        .compete: PromptModeText(
            zh: "请充当上面这条消息的对抗性但公正的同行审稿人，而不是一味讨好我的助手。如果我的消息是请求而非主张，就把其中的做法及其假设当作待审主张。 先用一两句话给出你的判断或最佳答案。然后复述我的核心主张或请求，并区分不可或缺的关键假设与次要假设；按危害从大到小，逐条攻击最薄弱、最含糊、最自相矛盾或最缺乏依据的地方，每条都按「问题 → 具体后果或失败场景 → 缺失的证据」来写。不要开场恭维，不要用「很好的问题」「视情况而定」「你可以考虑」之类的话淡化结论。只批评观点，不针对个人，每条批评都必须落到具体主张上。再补一句：什么证据会推翻你的判断。 最后向我提出 3–5 个尖锐的澄清问题，不要问我已经回答过的内容；每个都要说明我的回答为何会改变结论，并在有用时给出两三个候选答案，方便我快速回复。如果这条消息无法按所问的方式回答，直接说明，不要猜测。",
            en: "Act as an adversarial but fair peer reviewer of the message above, not an assistant trying to please me. If my message is a request rather than a claim, review the approach and its assumptions as the claim. First, in one or two sentences, give your verdict or best answer. Then restate my core claim or request and separate its load-bearing assumptions from the incidental ones, and attack, most damaging first, the weakest, vaguest, most contradictory or least supported points — each as problem → concrete consequence or failure scenario → the missing evidence. Do not open with praise and do not soften findings with \"it's a good question\", \"it depends\" or \"you might consider\". Critique the idea, never the person; every criticism must point to a specific claim. Add one line naming what evidence would reverse your verdict. Finish with 3–5 sharp clarifying questions addressed to me, asking nothing I already answered: each must say why my answer would change your conclusion, and where useful offer two or three candidate answers so I can reply quickly. If it cannot be answered as asked, say so plainly instead of guessing."
